# Project structure for website mockups

This repository holds functional website mockups guided by design. Follow this layout whenever creating a new project.

## New project folder

- Create a **root-level folder** named after the project (kebab-case), e.g. `kalos-dwellings-v2/`.
- Put all project pages, assets, CSS, and JS **inside that folder** — never scatter a project’s files across the repo root when working in the multi-project layout.
- Follow established design/system rules and the design guidance for that mockup.

## Project index (summary)

Inside each project folder, include an `index.html` that is the **summary / guide view** for that project:

- Title and short description of the project
- A clear list of **all important project links** (page-by-page guide, homepage/prototype, PDFs, etc.)
- Links must open in a new tab with `target="_blank"` and `rel="noreferrer noopener"`

### Link format example

```html
<a
  href="https://yeraysgonzalez.github.io/kalos-dwellings-v2/v2.html"
  rel="noreferrer noopener"
  title="https://yeraysgonzalez.github.io/kalos-dwellings-v2/v2.html"
  target="_blank"
>https://yeraysgonzalez.github.io/kalos-dwellings-v2/v2.html</a>
```

Prefer the live share URLs when they exist; otherwise use relative paths to pages inside the same project folder (still with `target="_blank"` and `rel="noreferrer noopener"`).

## Checklist for a new project

1. Create `/<project-name>/` at the repo root
2. Add `/<project-name>/index.html` as the summary with the full link list
3. Add the mockup pages and assets under that folder
4. Keep the summary updated when new pages or share links are added
